TITLE:: ReverbKit
summary:: the arithmetic the four reverbs share
categories:: Libraries>Reverbs
related:: Classes/Hall, Classes/Plate, Classes/Coil, Classes/Shimmer, Classes/FxLoop

DESCRIPTION::
Class methods used inside the reverbs' DSP: a stereo pair out of any number of channels and back, an allpass's decay time for a coefficient, the gain of one lap of a loop for a decay in seconds, and the feedback delay network link::Classes/Plate:: and link::Classes/Shimmer:: are built on. It is not an effect: SuperDirtGUI and FxChainPanel list the subclasses of link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, and this is not one.

code::
(
{
	var in = Impulse.ar(0) ! 2;
	ReverbKit.fdn(in, 1, 2, 8000, 100, 0.2) * 0.5
}.play;
)
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: pair
The two channels a reverb works on: the first and the last of what it was given, so a mono input goes to both.
ARGUMENT:: sig
An Array of channels, or one.

METHOD:: spread
The pair back onto n channels: one channel takes the middle of the two, more take the sides in turn.
ARGUMENT:: lr
A pair.
ARGUMENT:: n
How many channels.

METHOD:: apTime
AllpassC's decay time for a delay and a coefficient: the UGen takes the time of a 60 dB fall, and the coefficient raised to decay over delay is 0.001 there.
ARGUMENT:: delay
In seconds.
ARGUMENT:: k
The coefficient, 0 to 1.

METHOD:: lapGain
What one lap of a loop is scaled by, for a tail to reach 60 dB down in decay seconds.
ARGUMENT:: lap
The lap, in seconds.
ARGUMENT:: decay
The time, in seconds.

METHOD:: hadamard
The 4 x 4 Hadamard matrix applied to four signals, scaled so energy is kept.
ARGUMENT:: r
Four signals.

METHOD:: fdn
A feedback delay network of four lines, Hadamard mixed, inside a link::Classes/FxLoop::. Answers a pair.
ARGUMENT:: in2
A pair going in.
ARGUMENT:: room
Scales the lines: 1 is 42 to 73 ms.
ARGUMENT:: decay
Seconds to 60 dB.
ARGUMENT:: damp
The low pass in the loop, Hz.
ARGUMENT:: lowCut
The high pass in the loop, Hz.
ARGUMENT:: mod
How much the lines move, 0 to 1.
ARGUMENT:: hold
0 to 1: at 1 the lines go round at unity with the filters out, and nothing more comes in.
ARGUMENT:: maxRoom
The largest room the loop is sized for.
